{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-20314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A boat travels downstream on a river. The table below gives the speed $v(t)$, in miles per hour, of the boat at certain moments during its journey.\n\n| $t\\text{ (hours)}$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1$ | $1.3$ | $1.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v\\text{ (mi/hour) }$ | $32$ | $35$ | $40$ | $65$ | $80$ | $65$ |\n\n Use the right Riemann sum for $v(t)$ over $[0,1.5]$ with five subintervals to approximate the total distance traveled by the boat.\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the speed-time graph.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-20314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $A$ denote the area under the curve $y=v(t)$ over $[0,1.5].$ \nIn this case, we have $n=5$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the total distance traveled can be approximated as\n\n$$\nA≈v(0.3)Δ{t}_{1}+v(0.7)Δ{t}_{2}+v(1)Δ{t}_{3}+v(1.3)Δ{t}_{4}+v(1.5)Δ{t}_{5},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{t}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $t$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{t}_{i}={t}_{i}-{t}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δt$'s.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1$ | $1.3$ | $1.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δt$ | $-$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $v(t)$ | $-$ | $35$ | $40$ | $65$ | $80$ | $65$ |\n\nWe plug in the numbers to approximate the number of liters and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈35\\cdot 0.3+40\\cdot 0.4+65\\cdot 0.3+80\\cdot 0.3+65\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =10.5+16+19.5+24+13 \\\\  & =83.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total distance traveled by the boat. So, the distance is approximately $83\\,\\text{mi}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-20314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7459cac5ae294c20fddd3db48d5b8b36d078018fb7a0fc2f44a3712ec91ba34"} {"question" "q-20314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-20314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "70\\,\\text{mi}"] ["math" "75\\,\\text{mi}"] ["math" "80\\,\\text{mi}"] ["math" "81\\,\\text{mi}"] ["math" "83\\,\\text{mi}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-20314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "83\\,\\text{mi}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A right Riemann sum is used to approximate the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=-1$ and $x=1$ for each of the functions below. For which function does the Riemann sum give an *underestimate* of the area?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The right Riemann sum underestimates the area under the respective curve if the function is decreasing over the given interval. \n\nOf the given options, the only function that is decreasing over $x\\in [-1,1]$ is as follows.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/bd25af02c775675398a93df167cce72fa3ec50efe7bddb5c92bc7176571ee4dc.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7459cac5ae294c20fddd3db48d5b8b36d078018fb7a0fc2f44a3712ec91ba34"} {"question" "q-115698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/926dad6d4a567eeaebf5393a0b624f7d79c84b5a1b9d2409c26a3a7eaf2d4d38.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/b20771fe256aba4c1ea20f5014230eb8868b0aacda8e57a79d5b5263ff9f2259.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/bd21ae5295ae8d6c22d242f730f8b3b821cab8668d3d79f3b56a0ba0cb42797c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/bd25af02c775675398a93df167cce72fa3ec50efe7bddb5c92bc7176571ee4dc.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/f03ac639e6c013d192c41dcf4c28774e13080a109dd767990745745b17b97231.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/bd25af02c775675398a93df167cce72fa3ec50efe7bddb5c92bc7176571ee4dc.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A right Riemann sum is used to approximate the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=-1$ and $x=1$ for each of the functions below. For which function does the Riemann sum give an *overestimate* of the area?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The right Riemann sum overestimates the area under the respective curve if the function is increasing over the given interval. \n\nOf the given options, the only function that is increasing over $x\\in [-1,1]$ is as follows.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/d0e535f39c947e55b6dba151f723dd3390fe67c29a571b940294e90869acac21.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7459cac5ae294c20fddd3db48d5b8b36d078018fb7a0fc2f44a3712ec91ba34"} {"question" "q-115705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/156d711270f2d684a0cd0f432784b3380e08a55ff8f2dfd74f5b031bf61180db.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/5c1da597db0e430c01b29894cc47e7c5cece4a43d19e1da80321af7c7a80b9e3.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/60748a498e3d236138b7e028ab8f8ed58ab1d65657196e51bf2af9a328862cba.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/9089c51c94498929215e48e02cade4d69b900883793c9e56b38473e061f79f21.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/d0e535f39c947e55b6dba151f723dd3390fe67c29a571b940294e90869acac21.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/d0e535f39c947e55b6dba151f723dd3390fe67c29a571b940294e90869acac21.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The table below gives some values of a continuous function $f(x)$ on the closed interval $[-6,3].$ The right Riemann sum approximation to the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ with $3$ equal subintervals has a value of $6.$ What must be the value of $k?$\n\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $7$ | $5$ | $-2$ | $k$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area $A$ under the graph can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(-3)+f(0)+f(3)}})\\cdot {{Δx}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nLet's set up a table with the values of $f(x)$ at each point:\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $5$ | $-2$ | $k$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(5+(-2)+k)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =(k+3)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3k+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we are given that $A$ must be $6$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k+9 & =6 \\\\ 3k & =6-9 \\\\ k & =\\frac{-3}{3} \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7459cac5ae294c20fddd3db48d5b8b36d078018fb7a0fc2f44a3712ec91ba34"} {"question" "q-115737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-115737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-346457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The following table shows the values of a continuous function $f(x)$ over the interval $[10,16].$\n\n| $x$ | $10$ | $12$ | $13.5$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $7$ | $2$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nUse the right Riemann sum, with the three subintervals indicated by the data, to approximate the area $A$ under the curve $y=f(x)$ over the interval $[10,16].$ \n\n$A≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-346457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have $n=3$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the area is approximated as \n\n$$\nA≈f(12)Δ{x}_{1}+f(13.5)Δ{x}_{2}+f(16)Δ{x}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{x}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $x$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δx$'s.\n\n| $x$ | $10$ | $12$ | $13.5$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δx$ | $-$ | $2$ | $1.5$ | $2.5$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $2$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nFinally, we plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈2\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 1.5+3\\cdot 2.5 \\\\  & =4+6+7.5 \\\\  & =17.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-346457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7459cac5ae294c20fddd3db48d5b8b36d078018fb7a0fc2f44a3712ec91ba34"} {"question" "q-346457" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f3d6a878398b8da0ee45449a496289e73eb64538291434b45175f2afbbcb5fb"} {"question" "q-346457" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "17.5"] 